    "narrative": "For today's slate, our offensive engine is anchored by three high-efficiency starts. **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) stands as our top play, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Mahle and a substantial +14% platoon boost, while **Seiya Suzuki** (73.90) and **Brice Turang** (73.19) follow closely. **Seiya Suzuki** is bolstered by a significant BvP edge (+8%) and a prime spot in the two-hole, though he remains a watch-list item due to a 39% rain risk. **Brice Turang** earns his spot as a must-start not only for the soft matchup against Chandler but for his relentless stolen base utility, bolstered by a 100% stolen base success rate against this specific delivery profile. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains a locked-in core play, leveraging a strong park factor and a clean platoon advantage against Bradish.\n\nThe decision to bench **Josh Naylor** (53.42) was the most difficult pivot of the day, as his projection was nearly identical to that of **Edwin Arroyo** (53.25) and **Dalton Rushing** (53.32). Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the positional versatility and late-game stolen base leverage offered by **Dalton Rushing** and the defensive floor of **Edwin Arroyo**. We are monitoring the weather closely: **Edwin Arroyo** and **Seiya Suzuki** face moderate rain risks, and **Austin Riley** (54.86) is battling a \"Wind In\" penalty that slightly tempers his raw power projection against Liberatore. While **James Wood** (53.19) has a sub-3.00 xERA matchup against Schlittler, his elite xwOBA metrics keep him in the lineup despite the tough pitcher-hitter environment.",
